{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114555","id":3143376066,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc67XBzC","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114555","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114555.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114555.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114555","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114555/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114555/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114555/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/7e05ac99a8df66c6b1d193584d4414461062303f","number":114555,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Standardize paths used under drag and drop action in Windows platform specfically","user":{"login":"onequid","id":49135017,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5MTM1MDE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49135017?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/onequid","html_url":"https://github.com/onequid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/onequid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/onequid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/onequid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/onequid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/onequid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/onequid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/onequid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/onequid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/onequid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The paths of files/directories under drag-n-drop action from system file explorer to godot assets dock in Windows are standardized now.\r\n\r\nIt fixes the check here:\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/f0aeea26fb9d930be42f1cdc5cb55b3acf9589bf/core/io/dir_access.cpp#L413-L414\r\n\r\nThis also fixes the freeze of godot editor and duplicated tmp files after dragging and dropping files(assets) from OS File Explorer to where they already are, as is described here: \r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114218#issuecomment-3677105631\r\n\r\nAdditionally, `create_temp_dir`, which is used by `handle_filedescriptor_format`, also returns a standardized path string.\r\n\r\n---\r\n<details><summary>Update(Incapable)</summary>\r\n<p>\r\nThe `DirAccessWindows::is_equivalent(a, b)` function compared hard driver information of paths, namely volume serial number, LowPart, HighPart. \r\nOnly `DirAcessUnix` and `DirAccessWindows` implement the `is_equivalent(a, b)` function.\r\n`DirAcessUnix::is_equivalent(a, b)` is **NOT** tested yet, though it seems to work as it returns string comparison result if it failed checking file system ID.\r\n\r\nMarked the PR as draft, before a Unix test or approval.\r\n\r\nAnd though the `DirAccessWindows::is_equivalent(a, b)` formats both the given path arguements with `fix_path(p_path)` function, the calling of `simplify_path()` should remain as they should be standardized.\r\n</p>\r\n</details> \r\n\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":205417413,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMDU0MTc0MTM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/platform:windows","name":"platform:windows","description":"","color":"e4e4e4","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098255,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyNTU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:plat